# Campus Motion - Cursor rules

AGENTS.md at the repository root is the authoritative contract. Read it before writing code or answering architecture questions. Scoped rules live in .cursor/rules/*.mdc. Project skills live in .agents/skills/.

## Default behaviour on a pasted issue or screenshot

Do not ask the student for instructions. Run the pipeline in AGENTS.md section 5: decompose into layers, check lib/widgets/ for existing components, extract new visual components into lib/widgets/<name>.dart, compose the screen inside MasterContainer, map colours to AppColors, register routes in AppRoutes, run the checks, and output a branch name, commit message and PR description.

## Key invariants

1. Every top-level screen is wrapped in MasterContainer (450 px column).
2. Reuse widgets from lib/widgets/ (AppCard, AppButton, StatItem, ActivityCard, EventPreviewCard, NewsCard, SectionHeader) before writing UI.
3. Every screen is registered in AppRoutes (lib/config/routes.dart); navigate with Navigator.pushNamed.
4. Network calls only in lib/services/ through ApiService. Never call http from a screen. New endpoints get a MockDataService handler.
5. Backend is https://api.campusmotion.ch. Never add Firebase or analytics SDKs.
6. Health data (weight, height, birth date) needs explicit consent. New activities default to is_public: false.
7. After every await, check `if (!mounted) return;` before using BuildContext.
8. Use .withValues(alpha: ...) and SharePlus.instance.share(...).
9. No emoji in code, UI text, commits, PRs, issues or docs.
10. Before finishing, run from mobile_app/: dart format --output=none --set-exit-if-changed . ; flutter analyze --fatal-infos ; flutter test --coverage ; dart run tool/check_coverage.dart
